    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded in 681 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asparuh-of-bulgaria">Asparuh</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a> among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, it was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>'s chief Balkan rival for three centuries.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-i-of-bulgaria">Boris I</a>'s conversion in 864 and the schools of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/preslav">Preslav</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohrid">Ohrid</a> made it the cradle of Slavonic letters and Cyrillic.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simeon-i-of-bulgaria">Simeon I</a> (893–927) it dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> destroyed it after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kleidion">Battle of Kleidion</a> in 1014.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>After killing the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-i">Nikephoros I</a> in 811, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krum">Khan Krum</a> had the emperor's skull lined with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and used it as a drinking cup, according to Byzantine sources.</p></aside>
    </section>

