ia">Boris I</a> receives the disciples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyril-and-methodius">Cyril and Methodius</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">917</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simeon-i-of-bulgaria">Simeon I</a> crushes a Byzantine army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-achelous">Battle of Achelous</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">927</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> recognises Peter I as tsar and the Bulgarian patriarchate</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1014</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> destroys Samuel's army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kleidion">Battle of Kleidion</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1018</span><span class="rf-text">The Bulgarian nobles surrender to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohrid">Ohrid</a></span></li></ol>
